WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:04.950
Although Sony and Marvel Studios have shared
custody of Tom Holland's Spider-Man so that

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:09.710
he can exist in the Marvel Cinematic Universe
alongside the Avengers, the former studio

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:13.610
is still pushing ahead with its own universe
of Spidey villains and anti-heroes.

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:21.410
"Venom" was a surprise hit back in 2018, raking
in $856 million — so audiences are clearly

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:24.910
interested in Sony's edgy approach to superheroes.

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:29.190
It's no surprise, then, that the studio is
working on a solo "Kraven the Hunter" film

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:33.829
starring Aaron Taylor-Johnson, as well as
a "Madame Web" adventure with Dakota Johnson

00:00:33.829 --> 00:00:35.219
and Sydney Sweeney.

00:00:35.219 --> 00:00:40.879
Meanwhile, Jared Leto's "Morbius" is finally
set to arrive in theaters on April 1, and

00:00:40.879 --> 00:00:42.579
it's been a long time coming.

00:00:42.579 --> 00:00:47.980
The movie was originally intended to debut
on July 10, 2020, but that was delayed almost

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:52.789
immediately— and then the pandemic hit,
causing Sony to push the release back several

00:00:52.789 --> 00:00:53.789
more times.

00:00:53.789 --> 00:00:58.920
"Morbius" follows Leto as Dr. Michael Morbius,
a genius who is determined to find a cure

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:02.519
for the rare blood disorder that he's suffered
from since childhood.

00:01:02.519 --> 00:01:07.500
His research leads him to an experimental
procedure using bats, and it transforms him

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:13.920
into a vicious beast with the comic-accurate
gray skin and red eyes, enhanced senses, super-strength,

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:15.590
and the ability to fly.

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:21.060
Unfortunately, he also has to contend with
Matt Smith's Loxias Crown and FBI Agent Simon

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:23.210
Stroud, played by Tyrese Gibson.

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:27.380
The first reactions from critics have made
their way online, and they paint an interesting

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:30.340
picture of Sony's latest Marvel movie.

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:34.720
Collider contributor Sab Astley blasted the
movie for its poor story, tweeting,

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:37.310
"Morbius is about as bad as you were expecting.

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:43.280
A 2005 plot collides with visually confusing
CGI to create a bit of a snooze fest.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:46.000
But don't worry, they've saved the worst for
last.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:51.450
Featuring some of the worst post credits scenes
you've EVER seen, Sony are off their rocker."

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:56.090
The We Have a Hulk podcast's Nicola Austin
echoed the sentiment, noting that it doesn't

00:01:56.090 --> 00:01:59.140
live up to the "Venom" corner of Sony's Marvel
universe.

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:00.140
She posted,

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:07.150
"Well Morbius is unfortunately not great (some
really shoddy vfx &amp; 00s formulaic plot) &amp; definitely

00:02:07.150 --> 00:02:08.899
not as fun as Venom.

00:02:08.899 --> 00:02:12.929
Really confused at the future of the Sony
Spiderverse following the post-credits scenes

00:02:12.929 --> 00:02:14.030
&amp; the editing."

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:18.640
Meanwhile, Escape Film Club tweeted that the
film's visuals can't save it, posting,

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:23.680
"Morbius proves that no matter how many famous
faces or shiny visuals you squeeze in, Sony

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:27.819
will always find a way to impressively misunderstand
basic storytelling."

00:02:27.819 --> 00:02:30.780
Film critic Ren Viera followed that up, writing,

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:35.150
"Matt Smith gloriously hams up the place and
Oliver Wood delivers some visual flare to

00:02:35.150 --> 00:02:36.750
the action sequences.

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:42.799
Aside from that, the bad plotting &amp; messy
cgi, confusing editing &amp; worse sound mix result

00:02:42.799 --> 00:02:44.680
in absolute incoherence.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.900
But the post-credits manage to outdo it all."

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:50.819
One of the biggest questions fans have about
"Morbius" is: When is he going to meet the

00:02:50.819 --> 00:02:53.400
other Sony Marvel characters, like Venom?

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:57.829
Obviously, an earlier trailer reveals a look
at Michael Keaton's Vulture, which implies

00:02:57.829 --> 00:03:01.680
that a Sinister-Six style team-up is on the
way at some point.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:05.579
Sony has been keen to make a movie about the
squad of "Spider-Man" villains for quite some

00:03:05.579 --> 00:03:09.629
time, and the original plan was to spin it
out of "The Amazing Spider-Man" franchise.

00:03:09.629 --> 00:03:14.180
For the moment, it's not clear if, or when,
Morbius will cross over with the likes of

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:16.010
Venom, Vulture, or Kraven.

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:20.029
Although, Jared Leto previously told Screen
Rant that of all the Marvel characters the

00:03:20.029 --> 00:03:23.969
Living Vampire could meet, quote, "Venom would
make a lot of sense.

00:03:23.969 --> 00:03:24.969
That would be fun."

00:03:24.969 --> 00:03:28.299
It's worth pointing out that just because
the film has had a negative reaction from

00:03:28.299 --> 00:03:31.459
critics doesn't mean it won't be successful
at the box office.

00:03:31.459 --> 00:03:36.189
At the end of the day, if "Morbius" is hugely
profitable, then Sony will likely continue

00:03:36.189 --> 00:03:39.510
to use the character in sequels and crossovers.

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:43.540
Leto himself revealed on "The Late Late Show
with James Corden" that he could easily cross

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:45.609
over into the upcoming "Blade" movie.

00:03:45.609 --> 00:03:49.640
For now, it's probably best to go into "Morbius"
with a little caution.

